<%# How AIM works (#131, brought up to date in #187): by task, short answers,
    with screenshots where there are some (aim_help_shot; retaken with
    bin/aim-help-shots). %>
<% sections = {
     'start' => 'Getting around', 'roles' => 'Who can do what', 'groups' => 'Agency groups',
     'upload' => 'Uploading invoices', 'working' => 'Working an invoice', 'pdf' => 'Fixing a PDF', 'duplicates' => 'Possible duplicates',
     'find' => 'Find an invoice', 'older' => 'Finding an old invoice', 'waiting' => 'Waiting too long', 'fiscal' => 'Fiscal', 'stamp' => 'The approval stamp', 'setup' => 'Setting up a group', 'alerts' => 'Email alerts', 'faq' => 'Quick answers'
   } %>
<div class="aim-page aim-help">
  <header class="aim-page-header">
    <div>
      <h1 class="aim-page-title">How AIM works</h1>
      <p class="aim-page-subtitle">What each part of AIM is for, and how to do the common things.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="aim-help__toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <% sections.each do |anchor, title| %><%= link_to title, "##{anchor}" %><% end %>
  </nav>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="start">
    <h2>Getting around</h2>
    <p>Opening AIM takes you straight to your own dashboard: AIM Admins to the Dashboard (or My AIM if you start in
      Approver mode), Fiscal to the Fiscal Dashboard, anyone with a queue to My AIM.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dashboard</strong> (AIM Admins): <em>Find an invoice</em> at the top, then what needs a look first --
        possible duplicates, invoices to type in, second approvals, anything waiting over a week, failures -- a card per
        queue, today's movement, the invoices waiting longest, the <strong>Stale</strong> panel, and each agency group's
        share. Click any tile or card to open that list.</li>
      <li><strong>My AIM</strong> (everyone else with a queue): <em>Find an invoice</em> for your own invoices, your queue,
        what has waited over a week, your second approvals and anything for you to type in.</li>
      <li><strong>Fiscal Dashboard</strong> (Fiscal): the same for the Fiscal stage, with its own <em>Find an invoice</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>The AIM #</strong> (<em>AIM-118</em>) is an invoice's short number from the moment it arrives. It is on
        every list, on the review page next to the status, and on Fiscal's pages and reports; Find and Search older
        invoices take it too.</li>
      <li><strong>Pipeline counts</strong> in the sidebar are what is in each queue. Rejected and Deleted count what nobody
        has acknowledged yet; Finished, last, has no count.</li>
      <li><strong>Managing</strong>, top right on many pages, picks which agency group a page shows when you work more than
        one. It is remembered until you change it.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('dashboard', 'The Dashboard: needs attention, the queue cards, today, the oldest waiting.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="roles">
    <h2>Who can do what</h2>
    <table class="submission-table aim-people-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Set where</th><th>Can</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">AIM Admin</td><td>ACL (the aim_admin group)</td><td>Everything, in every group.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">Group Admin</td><td>Agency Groups &rsaquo; Group roles, or a person's profile</td>
            <td>Their group's people and BU Admins, its Fiscal people, settings, templates, reject reasons, second approvals
              and alerts. Also works its Fiscal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">Fiscal</td><td>The same</td><td>Their group's Fiscal stage, coding rules and lookup imports,
              report templates and reports; can upload straight to Fiscal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">BU Admin</td><td>A person's profile, or a group's BUs &amp; People</td>
            <td>Their BUs' people and shared queues.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">User</td><td>Users &amp; Queues</td><td>Approves what is in their queue and their BUs' shared queues.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="groups">
    <h2>Agency groups</h2>
    <p>An agency group decides who works Fiscal and the coding rules for a set of budget units, and how. Every agency AIM
      uses has its own group. A <strong>custom group</strong> takes some of an agency's BUs for itself -- say Sheriff
      Detention's units -- so they get their own Fiscal people and settings. Every BU is in exactly one group.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Make a custom group:</strong> Admin &rsaquo; Agency Groups &rsaquo; New custom group, then tick its BUs on
        its Budget units tab. They leave the agency's group; untick to send one back.</li>
      <li><strong>Which BUs AIM uses</strong> is the same setting on an agency's group and on AIM's Budget Units: untick a
        BU on either and AIM stops using it.</li>
      <li><strong>Fiscal also processes:</strong> on a group's Fiscal settings, tick other groups its Fiscal should work too.</li>
      <li><strong>Deleting:</strong> only a custom group can go; its BUs return to the agency's group.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('agency_group', 'A group, tab by tab: Budget units, BUs & People, Group roles, Fiscal settings, Alerts.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="upload">
    <h2>Uploading invoices</h2>
    <p>Upload Invoices asks two things: <strong>whose queue</strong> it goes to, and whether the AI reads it.</p>
    <table class="submission-table aim-people-table">
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>The AI reads it (default)</th><th>Skip the AI</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">A queue</td><td>The AI reads it, then it reaches the queue.</td>
            <td>Straight to the queue, flagged <em>Manual Data Entry Needed</em> until the details are typed in.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="is-strong">Straight to Fiscal</td><td>The AI reads it, then it is approved in your name and goes to
            Fiscal (Action Needed first if the AI has trouble).</td>
            <td>Straight to the Fiscal Queue, flagged; Fiscal types it in, then it is billed and filed.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <ul>
      <li>Anyone with a queue can skip the AI for their own queue; AIM Admins and that BU's Admins for anyone's.</li>
      <li>Straight to Fiscal is for AIM Admins and Fiscal (Fiscal for their groups' BUs). It names you as the approver.</li>
      <li>Every invoice is billed, however it came in.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('upload', 'Upload: whose queue, and Skip the AI.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="working">
    <h2>Working an invoice</h2>
    <p>The buttons sit in one row under the fields: on the right <strong>Save Changes</strong> and the one main action for
      where the invoice is (<em>Send to Approval</em>, <em>Approve</em>, <em>Approve Split</em>, <em>Retry AI</em> or
      <em>Retry Export</em>); on the left <strong>More</strong> for the rest -- Retry AI, Send to a queue, and Reject and
      Delete in red. Each still asks first.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Approve</strong> sends it to billing and Fiscal. Over its BU's second-approval amount, the button says
        <em>Approve (first of two)</em> and it goes on to the BU's second approver, who approves it or uses
        <em>Return to first approver</em>. The approval stamp names both.</li>
      <li><strong>Send Back</strong> when the invoice is fine but AIM read it wrong or something is missing: it returns to
        AIM review.</li>
      <li><strong>Reject</strong> when it should not be paid through AIM at all -- not an invoice, not ours, a duplicate.
        Pick a reason or Other and type one. A copy goes back to the submitter.</li>
      <li><strong>Move</strong> when it belongs in someone else's queue. AIM Admins also have <strong>Send to a queue</strong>
        from anywhere the AI is not working on it, optionally flagged for data entry.</li>
      <li><strong>Manual Data Entry Needed</strong>: type the details in from the PDF and Save; the flag clears once what an
        approval needs is in.</li>
      <li><strong>Restore</strong> (on a rejected or deleted invoice's page): back to Action Needed, or straight to its
        owner, with a reason.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('review', 'The review page: the PDF, the fields, and the buttons.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="pdf">
    <h2>Fixing an invoice's PDF</h2>
    <p><strong>Edit PDF</strong>, above the PDF on the review page and on Fiscal's page, turns the preview into an editor.
      Nothing changes until <em>Apply changes</em>; <em>Cancel</em> puts the preview back.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pages:</strong> the strip on the left -- click a page to see it big, drag to reorder. <em>Turn left</em>,
        <em>Turn right</em>, <em>Remove page</em> (greyed until you Apply; <em>Keep page</em> brings it back), and
        <em>Add pages from a PDF</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>Crop:</strong> drag a box over what to keep, then drag its edges, corners or middle to adjust it.
        <em>Fit page</em>, <em>Fit width</em>, - and + zoom; dragging past the edge stops at the page.</li>
      <li><strong>Text:</strong> click the page to add a box and type. Drag its top bar to move it and its corner to resize;
        click in it any time to change the words. Size, bold, colour, a white or yellow background, a border, or delete it.</li>
      <li><strong>Swap the whole PDF</strong> for a corrected or cleaned copy from the vendor.</li>
      <li><strong>It stays editable.</strong> Every change is kept as a version, so Edit PDF opens where the last person
        left it -- their text boxes still boxes, removed pages there to keep again -- until Fiscal archives the invoice.</li>
      <li><strong>Versions</strong> lists every change: who, when and what. <em>View</em> any; <em>Restore</em> one to make it
        current again (that is a new version too, so nothing is lost).</li>
      <li>The AI does not read it again unless you tick <em>Read it again with the AI</em>; the invoice keeps its fields,
        queue and owner. On an approved invoice the approval stamp is redone; saved Fiscal reports keep their copy.</li>
      <li>Not while the AI or the export has it, nor once it is rejected, deleted, split or archived by Fiscal.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('pdf_editor', 'Edit PDF: the page strip, a text box with its toolbar, and the Versions menu.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="duplicates">
    <h2>Possible duplicates</h2>
    <p>An invoice with the same vendor, invoice number and total as an earlier one (ignoring case and spaces) goes to
      Action Needed as <em>Possible duplicate</em>, linked to the other. AIM staff choose, with the buttons on its red banner:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Reject as duplicate</strong> -- rejected, naming the other.</li>
      <li><strong>Replacement</strong> -- it replaces the other; both say so, with links.</li>
      <li><strong>Not a duplicate</strong> -- it carries on; it is not flagged again unless its vendor, number or total change.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="find">
    <h2>Find an invoice</h2>
    <p>The box at the top of the AIM Dashboard (and of the Fiscal Dashboard, for Fiscal) finds any invoice, whatever queue
      it is in.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Type an <strong>AIM #</strong> (<em>AIM-118</em>) to open that invoice, or any part of the vendor, the invoice # or
        the batch id, or an exact amount. One match opens straight away; several are listed with where each one is.</li>
      <li><strong>More filters:</strong> where it is, owner, budget unit, agency, the dates it was received between, manual
        data entry, possible duplicate, and stale.</li>
      <li>You only find what you could already open: AIM Admins, the groups picked in Managing; anyone else, their own
        invoices; Fiscal, their groups' invoices with Fiscal.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('find', 'Find an invoice: one list across every queue, each with where it is.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="older">
    <h2>Finding an old invoice</h2>
    <p><strong>Finished</strong> and Fiscal's <strong>Archived</strong> show what finished in the last 30 days. Pick
      another window (7, 30, 90 or 365 days) above the list. Nothing is moved or removed; older invoices are only out of
      view. Fiscal's <strong>Exported</strong> always shows everything: each invoice there is still waiting to be archived
      once paid.</p>
    <p><strong>Rejected</strong> and <strong>Deleted</strong> show what nobody has acknowledged yet, however old, and the
      sidebar counts them. <strong>Acknowledge</strong> one (on its row or its page), or tick several -- or the box in the
      heading for all -- and <em>Acknowledge selected</em>. It leaves the list for everyone, with a line in its history.
      Restoring an invoice clears its acknowledgement, so if it is rejected again it comes back.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Search older invoices</strong> looks through every finished invoice, of all time: vendor (any part of the
        name), invoice # (any part), amount (exact, <em>1,234.50</em> or <em>$1234.5</em>), budget unit, agency, and the
        dates it finished between. Pick the list to search in Status.</li>
      <li>Dates alone browse a period, e.g. everything rejected in March.</li>
      <li>A search shows at most <%= Aim::ArchiveSearch::CAP %> invoices, newest first; past that it says to narrow the search.</li>
      <li>Managing applies, as on every list. <em>Back to recent</em> returns to the window.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('older', 'Search older invoices on Finished, with the window above the list.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="waiting">
    <h2>Waiting too long</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every invoice still being worked shows its age as a pill on its row: how long since it arrived
        (<em>12 days</em>). When it reached its queue or changed hands more recently, the pill says that too
        (<em>32 days · 3 here</em>), so the person holding it now can see they only just got it.</li>
      <li>It turns red once it is stale: <%= pluralize(Aim::Waiting.stale_days, 'day') %> old. Age is what counts, so
        moving an invoice to another queue does not make it new again.</li>
      <li>The dashboard's <strong>Stale</strong> panel lists stale invoices by queue and whoever holds them now. Nothing is
        moved or removed because it is old; someone has to act on it.</li>
      <li><strong>Deleted invoices' PDFs</strong> can be purged after a retention period (<%= pluralize(Aim::DeletedPdfPurge.retention_days, 'day') %>),
        <%= Aim::DeletedPdfPurge.enabled? ? 'every night' : 'once it is switched on (it is not yet)' %>. The invoice's
        record and history stay, marked <em>PDF purged</em>, and it can no longer be restored. Rejected invoices are
        never purged.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('waiting', 'Action Needed: each row shows how long it has waited.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="fiscal">
    <h2>Fiscal</h2>
    <p>Every approved invoice reaches its group's Fiscal: <strong>Fiscal Queue</strong> (fill in pay doc, check, coding)
      &rarr; <strong>On Hold</strong> when waiting on something &rarr; <strong>Report Queue</strong> &rarr;
      <strong>Exported</strong> once in a report &rarr; <strong>Archived</strong> once paid.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The report:</strong> tick invoices in the Report Queue, pick a template, <em>Preview report</em>. Then
        <em>Download only</em> for a draft (nothing changes), or <em>Download and process</em> to save it as a numbered
        report, move the invoices to Exported and note it in each one's history.</li>
      <li><strong>Reports</strong> lists every saved report: download it again exactly as made, or <em>Regenerate</em> it
        from the invoices' values now as a new number. Files are kept a year.</li>
      <li><strong>Report Templates:</strong> save named layouts -- columns ticked, dragged into order, renamed; comma or tab.</li>
      <li><strong>Group settings</strong> (Fiscal settings tab): the Default report, hold reasons, tags, fields needed
        before Archive, reject reasons.</li>
      <li><strong>On an invoice's Fiscal page:</strong> Hold, Release or Back to Fiscal Queue on the left of the button row,
        then Save and the main step -- <em>Add to Report Queue</em> or <em>Archive</em>. <strong>Edit PDF</strong> is there
        too, until it is archived.</li>
      <li><strong>Find an invoice</strong> on the Fiscal Dashboard searches every Fiscal list at once.</li>
    </ul>
    <%= aim_help_shot('fiscal_dashboard', 'The Fiscal Dashboard: needs attention, a card per Fiscal list, the longest waiting.') %>
    <%= aim_help_shot('fiscal_preview', 'The report preview, with Download only and Download and process.') %>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="stamp">
    <h2>The approval stamp</h2>
    <p>When an invoice is approved, AIM writes a stamp on a copy of its PDF: by default, bottom right of every page, the
      date it arrived and its invoice date, then who approved it and when. The PDF as received is kept unchanged.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stamp Layouts</strong> (Fiscal sidebar) is where a group's Fiscal change their group's stamp, and AIM
        Admins any group's and the default for groups without their own.</li>
      <li><strong>One stamping, any number of areas.</strong> The approval text, Fiscal's processing block (Budget Unit #,
        Account #, Initial, Date Processed), anything else: <em>Add stamp area</em> for each. All are written together.</li>
      <li><strong>Placing an area:</strong> drag it on the page; pull its right edge to set its width. It keeps to the
        nearest corner or edge (<em>Kept to</em>), so an area put bottom right stays bottom right on letter, legal, landscape
        and turned pages. <em>Turn</em> sets it at an angle in steps of 45 degrees; <em>Prints on</em> picks every page, the
        first or the last.</li>
      <li><strong>Preview on</strong> one of the group's recent invoices, or <em>Upload a PDF</em> of your own: it is only
        shown and checked, never kept. Every page shows, in a pane that scrolls on its own; <strong>−</strong>, <strong>+</strong>
        and <em>Fit</em> zoom it.</li>
      <li><strong>Making room:</strong> <em>Shrink page contents</em> shrinks the invoice itself on the stamped copy (to 95%
        down to 70%) and moves it to the centre, top, bottom, left or right, leaving a clear margin for the stamp. The
        stamp is never shrunk, and the PDF as received is never changed.</li>
      <li><strong>What it says:</strong> its rows, one per line, with fields from <em>Insert a field</em> (<em>Approved by</em> puts in
        <code>{approver}</code>). A date field takes the format picked beside it. <em>Insert a separator</em> puts in a
        separator like <code>[ _ ]</code> that prints only when the field after it has a value, so
        <code>{approver}[ _ ]{program}</code> never ends in a stray underscore. A row whose fields are all empty is left
        out, so a second-approval row only prints when there is one.</li>
      <li><strong>How it looks:</strong> Helvetica, Times or Courier (the fonts every PDF reader has), size, colour, bold,
        italic, alignment, line spacing, a border, and a background: solid, 75%, 50%, 25% or clear.</li>
      <li><strong>Safety nets:</strong> an area grows into the page, never off it; it is pushed back inside if dragged out;
        text wraps to its width, and shrinks if it is still too tall. Text is never cut off. A layout that would not fit
        a page even at the smallest size cannot be saved. The designer also warns when an area sits over printing.</li>
      <li><strong>Fill with</strong> picks what the fields show, in the designer and in Check alike: <em>This invoice</em>
        (exactly what the invoice picked would print -- rows it has no values for yet are left out), <em>Samples</em> (a
        real coding rule of the group's agency, with sample names and dates), or <em>Longest values</em> (every field at
        the longest it has been in AIM, to see a layout at its fullest). An uploaded PDF has no invoice, so it takes
        samples.</li>
      <li><strong>Check</strong> has the server stamp the invoice picked, or your uploaded PDF, with the layout as it
        stands, through the same code that stamps approvals, and opens the result in a new tab. Nothing is saved.</li>
      <li><strong>Saving</strong> keeps every version (History; <em>Load</em> opens an old one) and asks which invoices take
        it: those still with Fiscal (Fiscal Queue, On Hold, Report Queue) are stamped again, or only new approvals. If a
        safety net was needed on an invoice, its Fiscal page says so next to the stamp.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="setup">
    <h2>Setting up a group</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Budget units:</strong> tick the BUs it serves.</li>
      <li><strong>Group roles:</strong> add its Group Admins and Fiscal people.</li>
      <li><strong>BUs &amp; People:</strong> add people to each BU, switch shared queues, appoint BU Admins, and set a BU's
        second approval (amount, starting at 25,000, and a second approver).</li>
      <li><strong>Fiscal settings:</strong> the Default report's columns and format, hold and reject reasons, tags, what
        Archive needs, and which other groups its Fiscal also processes.</li>
      <li><strong>Alerts:</strong> who is emailed about what (see below).</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="alerts">
    <h2>Email alerts</h2>
    <p><strong>Not sending yet</strong> -- they wait on Paperboy's email setup. A group's Alerts tab sets who would be
      emailed about what and shows who would be emailed today. A BU's own settings replace its group's whole; <em>Use the
      group's</em> puts it back.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Owners: invoices in their queue longer than 7 days (on); new invoices in their queue (off).</li>
      <li>BU Admins: possible duplicates; unowned shared-queue invoices older than 7 days.</li>
      <li>Second approvers: when a high-dollar invoice reaches them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="aim-panel aim-agency-group-panel aim-help__section" id="faq">
    <h2>Quick answers</h2>
    <dl class="aim-help__faq">
      <dt>I can't see an invoice I expect.</dt>
      <dd>Check Managing at the top right, and the agency group its BU is in. Fiscal and Coding Rules show only your groups.</dd>
      <dt>Approve says it is waiting for someone's second approval.</dt>
      <dd>It is over its BU's amount and has its first approval; only the BU's second approver (or AIM staff) can finish it.</dd>
      <dt>Add to Report Queue refuses.</dt>
      <dd>It was uploaded straight to Fiscal and still needs its details typed in; the banner lists what is missing.</dd>
      <dt>Archive is greyed out.</dt>
      <dd>The group needs some fields filled in first (Fiscal settings &rsaquo; Needed before archive); the label says which.</dd>
      <dt>Two invoices are flagged as duplicates but are not.</dt>
      <dd>AIM staff click <em>Not a duplicate</em>; it will not be flagged again unless its details change.</dd>
      <dt>How do I get a report again?</dt>
      <dd>Fiscal &rsaquo; Reports: Download gives the exact file as made (for a year); Regenerate makes a new one from today's values.</dd>
      <dt>A rejected or deleted invoice is gone from the list.</dt>
      <dd>Someone acknowledged it; its history says who. <em>Search older invoices</em> still finds it.</dd>
      <dt>An invoice I finished months ago is not in the list.</dt>
      <dd>The finished lists show the last 30 days; use <em>Search older invoices</em> above the list.</dd>
      <dt>A deleted invoice's PDF is gone.</dt>
      <dd>It was purged after the retention period; its record and history are still there.</dd>
      <dt>I changed an invoice's PDF and want the old one back.</dt>
      <dd>Edit PDF &rsaquo; Versions: View the one you want, then Restore it.</dd>
      <dt>Text someone added to a PDF is wrong.</dt>
      <dd>Edit PDF, click in the text box and change it, or select it and Delete box; then Apply changes.</dd>
      <dt>Where is the invoice's AIM #?</dt>
      <dd>Next to its status at the top of its page, in the AIM # column of every list, and on Fiscal's pages.</dd>
      <dt>AIM opened on a dashboard, not the front page.</dt>
      <dd>It opens where you work: AIM Admins on the Dashboard, Fiscal on the Fiscal Dashboard, others on My AIM.</dd>
      <dt>Why didn't anyone get an email?</dt>
      <dd>Email alerts are not switched on yet.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</div>
